<newsitem itemid="139869" id="root" date="1996-10-24" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fidelity Bank lifts yr shr 28 percent.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Bank lifts yr shr 28 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended September 30</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    195.2	   vs 152.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)    46.0 making 67.0	    vs 54.0</p>
<p>    Net income		   41.02	   vs 30.95</p>
<p>    Net interest income	99.23	   vs 87.76</p>
<p>    Other operating income   17.76	   vs 14.41</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 16.79	   vs 16.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			62.80	   vs 48.12</p>
<p>    Tax			    21.78	   vs 17.17</p>
<p>Div payable December 4</p>
<p>On register November 8</p>
<p>Full name: Fidelity Bank Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The  bank said significant contributions to profit came from a return to historical asset growth trends, tight cost controls, a satisfactory bad debt ratio and higher productivity.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
